  "rationale": "The batch shows a structural gap at the end of an introductory prepositional time phrase: the model strongly favors a period after a noun, while the observed phrase ending in “On a sunny day” takes a comma. Add a rule for that reusable phrase shape rather than copying the particular adjective or noun. The title-shaped opening “det + adjective(s) + noun” is followed by a paragraph break in the batch, so add a narrowly scoped rule for that opening pattern. Initial A and The both occur as valid determiner starts (including A in replay), so give each modest initial-context support rather than asserting one required opening. Add modest support for a connective after a paragraph break and for an adjective after a determiner. These rules may overpredict commas after other On-phrases, paragraph breaks after noun phrases, or particular lexical choices; they add evidence without making alternatives impossible.",
